# The image needs the package and its dependency list, and nothing else in the
# repository — the rest is for developing it, and shipping documentation into a
# runtime image puts it where `docker export` can read it long after the
# repository has moved on. LICENSE and NOTICE are the deliberate exception; the
# Dockerfile says why they travel with the distribution.
*
!requirements.txt
!fastmcp_proxy/
!LICENSE
!NOTICE

# The runtime config is per deployment and mounted, never baked.
fastmcp_proxy/bridge.yaml
**/__pycache__/
